From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: brennoflavio <contato@brennoflavio.com.br>
Date: Wed, 14 Oct 2026 19:02:06 -0300
Subject: [PATCH] webapi: mock ordinary-page Chrome namespace natively

Expose per-realm window.chrome from the Window-only V8 snapshot before
page scripts and interface constructors. Use ordinary namespace objects,
not a Chrome interface, and leave extension-only runtime APIs absent.

Model the Chrome 155 uninstalled app surface: native non-constructible
methods, enums, no-op isInstalled setter, argument errors, and an async
installState callback owned by the context scheduler. csi/loadTimes are
anonymous constructible native functions with fresh plain-object results,
native data property descriptors and no-op setters. Keep result backing
values in V8 private properties, not host-object internal fields, so
structured cloning, messaging and native argument validation remain safe.

Record per-document wall/monotonic clock anchors and actual response-start,
DOMContentLoaded-end and load-end timestamps. Preserve navigation kinds;
read ALPN while the TLS connection is live rather than equating negotiation
with HTTP/2. No renderer, app installation or extension host is added; paint
and alternate-protocol observations remain zero/false in this mock.

Reference contract is pinned to Chromium 155.0.8059.40:
- chrome/renderer/loadtimes_bindings.cc
- chrome/renderer/extensions/api/app_hooks_delegate.cc
- content/public/renderer/chrome_object_extensions_utils.cc
https://chromium.googlesource.com/chromium/src/+/155.0.8059.40/
Supplemental desktop Chrome 154 introspection verified descriptors,
constructibility, optional callback arguments and native setter behavior;
it is not claimed to be a macOS reference execution.

Temporary diagnostics cover namespace/function descriptors, iframe
navigation, worker absence, GC/retained values, structuredClone and
MessageChannel delivery, slow-body response timing, HTTP/1.1 with/without
ALPN and HTTP/2. No new unit tests or benchmark predicates are added.
